  "not_covered": [
    "CPU only (8 forced CPU devices in one process); no TPU and no GPU.",
    "Single process and single host; no jax.distributed.initialize, no multi-host run, and no real distributed JAX.",
    "Orbax's own checkpoint is OCDBT/TensorStore on a local filesystem; the WeftFS store is a separate format. The comparison measures two independent implementations, not interchangeable files.",
    "Orbax features not exercised: Zarr3, per-leaf save_args/restore_args, transforms, custom metadata, step metadata contents, retention/deletion internals, emergency checkpointing, multi-axis meshes, and dtypes outside the exact WEFT-TENSOR v1 set.",
    "No process crash, power loss, or media failure during an Orbax save.",
    "Synthetic random weights, warm caches, one run; timings are not a fleet or production claim.",
    "The adapter's save pause is the time until Orbax's AsyncCheckpointer returns; the actual copy/store work runs on Orbax's background commit thread via a bounded worker."
